# 🔐 Password Strength Checker (CLI Tool)

A simple, clean **Command Line Interface (CLI)** tool written in **Python** to check password strength and generate strong passwords.

This project focuses on **clear logic, user-friendly output, and practical validation rules** — similar to what you'd expect in real-world utilities.

---

## ✨ Features

* ✅ Check password strength (WEAK / STRONG)
* 📊 Detailed password report:

  * Length (minimum 8 characters)
  * Uppercase letters
  * Lowercase letters
  * Numbers
  * Special symbols
* 💡 Smart suggestions to improve weak passwords
* 🔐 Generate strong random passwords
* 🖥️ Clean CLI menu & readable output

---

## 🧠 How It Works

The tool analyzes the entered password against common security rules:

| Rule      | Description                                |
| --------- | ------------------------------------------ |
| Length    | At least 8 characters                      |
| Uppercase | Contains A–Z                               |
| Lowercase | Contains a–z                               |
| Numbers   | Contains digits 0–9                        |
| Symbols   | Contains special characters like @ # $ % & |

If all rules pass → **STRONG** 💪
Otherwise → **WEAK** 😕 with suggestions.

---

## ▶️ Usage

Run the script from the terminal:

```bash
python3 proff_pass_check.py
```

### Menu Options

```
1- Check password strength
2- Generate strong password
3- Exit
```

---

## 🖥️ Example Output

```
Password report 📦
-------------------
Strength : WEAK 😕

Details :
❌ Length : 6 characters
❌ Uppercase letter
✅ Lowercase letter
✅ Numbers
❌ Special Symbols

Suggestion to improve your password :
• Use at least 8 characters
• Add at least one UPPERCASE letter
• Add at least one symbol like @ # $ % &
```

